# Single Project ID Environment Variable — No Backward Compatibility
RULE: Use GCP_PROJECT_ID everywhere. GCP_PROJECT_ID is REMOVED — no exceptions, no config.py workarounds.
WHY: Backward compatibility causes bugs in dev/prod environment switching. Clean break required.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/README.md#configuration
DO: Replace any GCP_PROJECT_ID with GCP_PROJECT_ID across all files including config classes
NEVER: GCP_PROJECT_ID anywhere — not even in config.py, not even as AliasChoices
ENFORCED BY: quality-gates codex compliance check (blocks merge)
See also: `no-backward-compatibility.mdc` for the general principle.

## Audit criteria
- **Correct:** `GCP_PROJECT_ID` only.
- **Banned:** `GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT` (deprecated GCP default), `GCP_PROJECT` (without `_ID`), or any variant that is NOT `GCP_PROJECT_ID`.
